WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
A joint is a fracture without appreciable displacement along

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.680 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
its surface. Cooling, unloading, or stress can create joints.

3
00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:10.820 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
A fault requires relative displacement. Trace a marker layer

4
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.800 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
across the break. The hanging wall lies above this

5
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.900 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
inclined plane. Move it down relative to the footwall:

6
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:21.240 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
a normal fault, commonly associated with extension. Move it

7
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:25.180 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
up: a reverse fault, commonly associated with shortening. A

8
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:28.160 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
thrust is a low-angle reverse fault. In map view,

9
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.220 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
the blocks slide horizontally. Matching markers become offset across

10
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:36.280 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
a strike-slip fault. Read relative motion; cliff height alone

11
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.080 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
does not identify the fault type.
